  "text": " נגיש\n\nincible装备\n\nincible装备\n\n\nLet $z = x + yi$, where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers. Then we have\n\n$\\|z^2 - 9\\| = \\|(x + yi)^2 - 9\\| = |x^2 - y^2 - 9 + 2xyi\\| = \\sqrt{(x^2 - y^2 - 9)^2 + (2xy)^2}$\n\nand\n\n$\\|z(z - 3i)\\| = \\|z^2 - 3zi\\| = |x^2 - y^2 - 3xi - 9i\\| = \\sqrt{(x^2 + y^2 - 9)^2 + (3x)^2}$\n\nSetting these equal gives\n\n$\\sqrt{(x^2 - y^2 + 9)^2 + (2xy)^2} = \\sqrt{(x^2 + y^2 - 9)^2 + (3x)^2}$\n\nSquaring both sides and simplifying gives\n\n$(x^2 - y^2 + 9)^2 + 4x^2y^2 = (x^2 + y^2 - 9)^2 + 9x^2$\n\nThis simplifies to $16x^2y^2 - 18x^2y^2 + 18x^2 + 9y^2 = 18x^2$\n\nWhich further simplifies to $y^2(16 - 18) = 0$\n\nThus, $16 - 18 = -2$, which is not equal to zero.\n\nTherefore, $x^2y^2 = 4x^2/18 = 2x/9$, or $y^2 = 2/9$.\n\nThe minimum value of $z$ occurs when $|z - 2i|$ is minimized, which is when $z = 2i$. Plugging this into the equation for $|z - 2i|$, we get\n\n$\\|2i - 2i\\| = \\|0 - 2i\\| = |2i| = \\boxed{2}$\n\n1 units.",
